 $('carbon-fixed-inputs').textContent=`Archived coefficients: density ${engineering.carbonCoefficients.density_kg_mm3*1e9} kg/m³; fuel factor ${engineering.roadReference.combustion_kg_CO2e_L+engineering.roadReference.supply_kg_CO2e_L} kg CO₂e/L (combustion plus supply); wire energy ${engineering.carbonCoefficients.edm.electricity_kJ_per_mm3_kerf} kJ/mm³ of kerf; wire removal ${engineering.carbonCoefficients.edm.material_removal_mm3_min} mm³/min; water allocation ${engineering.carbonCoefficients.edm.allocated_deionised_water_input_L_h} L/h; wire feed ${engineering.carbonCoefficients.edm.wire_feed_m_min} m/min. Grid and fuel-saving values are retained research inputs, not live national factors.`;
 const statusRows=[['Geometry and load compatibility','Checked against retained cases','Different dimensions, loads or histories require new supporting calculations.'],['Stress and fatigue reference','Case-linked screening-mesh numerical evidence','Exact-case mesh refinement and matched steel validation.'],['Prediction uncertainty','Conditional sensitivity available; no calibrated capacity bound','Quantify numerical, input, material and model uncertainty.'],['Gear-tooth bending rating','ISO 6336 rating not calculated','Mating gear, geometry factors, quality, load distribution, duty and material rating inputs.'],['Contact and pitting capacity','Mating contact not resolved','Contact geometry, lubrication, surface condition and a suitable rating/contact assessment.'],['Production fatigue','Component test not completed','Representative manufactured steel gears and documented loading history.'],['Manufacturing capability','Curvature screen and declared route arithmetic','Tool reach, tolerances, residual stress, machine stability and measured energy.'],['Climate comparison','Same-geometry scenario calculation','Measured inventory and documented service/replacement assumptions.'],['Full LCA / EPD / water impact','Not established','Complete applicable inventory, impact methods, interpretation and required review.']];
 $('assessment-status').innerHTML=statusRows.map(r=>'<tr>'+r.map(v=>'<td>'+esc(v)+'</td>').join('')+'</tr>').join('');
 const errorRows=Object.entries(engineering.empiricalErrors).map(([k,v])=>[k,v.observations,fmt(v.minimumSignedPercent,2)+' to '+fmt(v.maximumSignedPercent,2),fmt(v.p95AbsolutePercent,2),fmt(v.maximumAbsolutePercent,2)]);
 $('model-evidence').innerHTML=table(['Formulation','Related response rows','Signed error range (%)','P95 absolute (%)','Maximum absolute (%)'],errorRows)+`<p>The sample contains ten selected geometries with five related mixtures each. These are comparisons with numerical references, not a probability distribution of production capacity. Model E remains the primary registered formulation; H is secondary. E’s 46-tooth P95 criterion miss remains in the evidence section.</p><p>Conditional interval: [F̂/(1+ε), F̂/(1−ε)], if the assumed pointwise relative-error bound holds. The separate mesh study reports final-step retention changes up to 2.60% statically and 2.12% in fatigue on four other matched geometries; those changes are not a bound for every case.</p><p>Primary retention equation: R̂ = 1 / [1 + exp(θfamily) φⁿ b<sub>R</sub><sup>−m</sup> exp(c(λ−0.5))]. φ is opening area divided by the reference-annulus area; b<sub>R</sub> is root-side ligament divided by whole tooth height. The harmonic formulation combines separately predicted T/P capacities using the matched solid anchor factors.</p><a class="subtle-link" href="data/frozen-models.json" download>Full frozen equations, coefficient order and values ↓</a><p><a href="https://www.iso.org/standard/63819.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ISO 6336-1 · gear load-capacity framework</a> · <a href="https://www.asme.org/codes-standards/find-codes-standards/standard-for-verification-and-validation-in-computational-solid-mechanics" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ASME V&amp;V 10 · computational-model credibility</a></p>`;
 form.elements.project.addEventListener('input',()=>{updateReport();lockExports();});
